        <h2>Solar Energy Initiative</h2>
        <p>TPRS Glass has installed 1.3 MW of solar power and is expanding with an additional 6 MW under progress, targeting 80% of total electricity from renewable sources.</p>
        <p class="sustain-initiative__quote">Empowering our future: TPRS Glass drives toward 80% clean energy with 7.3 MW solar installations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sustain-initiative reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="80">
        <h2>Water Conservation and Management</h2>
        <p>TPRS Glass employs advanced Sewage Treatment Plants (STP) and Effluent Treatment Plants (ETP), each processing 20,000 liters per cycle to maximize water reuse and minimize environmental impact.</p>
        <p class="sustain-initiative__quote">Every drop counts: 40,000 L/cycle water recycled through STP &amp; ETP, powering a sustainable tomorrow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sustain-initiative reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="160">
        <h2>Responsible Sourcing Practices</h2>
        <p>TPRS Glass sources all process inks organically and eco-consciously, ensuring every material used is non-toxic, biodegradable, and environmentally safe.</p>
        <p class="sustain-initiative__quote">From source to solution: TPRS Glass guarantees 100% organic, eco-friendly inks for a safer world.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sustain-initiative reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="240">
        <h2>Recycling and Circularity</h2>
        <p>All glass waste at TPRS Glass is systematically collected and recycled, supporting a closed-loop system that prioritizes zero landfill and maximum material recovery.</p>
        <p class="sustain-initiative__quote">Closing the loop: Every shard of glass transformed, recycled, and reborn — nothing goes to waste at TPRS Glass.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

